From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: add a JPEG encoder

The H.264 encoder block of the engine also encodes baseline JPEG: the
encode mode field of its trigger register selects JPEG, the JPEG fields
of 0xb04 (pad the last scan byte with ones, stuff a zero after 0xff, the
DC biases) and the quantisation tables written through the block's
internal memory port (0xbe0/0xbe4: luma then chroma, natural order, the
rounding offset and the reciprocal of each quantiser) are documented in
the linux-sunxi VE register guide. The engine writes the entropy coded
scan with the Annex K Huffman tables; it does not write the headers.

Expose it as a third video device on the engine's M2M device,
"cedrus-jpeg-enc", a stateful JPEG encoder like the Hantro one, which
existing userspace drives without changes (GStreamer v4l2jpegenc): a raw
picture on the OUTPUT queue gives one JPEG image on the CAPTURE queue,
at the quality of V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY (the IJG scaling of
the Annex K tables), without requests; V4L2_ENC_CMD_STOP drains the
queue, the image of the last picture carries V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST. The
jobs share the engine's job queue with the decoder and the H.264
encoder.

The driver writes SOI, a JFIF APP0, DQT, SOF0 (4:2:0), DHT and SOS into
the coded buffer, padded with a comment segment to a multiple of 256
bytes, the granularity of the coded buffer address; the engine writes
the scan from there, and the driver ends it with EOI. Sizes 16x16 to
4096x4096 (the engine has no line buffer to size in JPEG mode). Whether
the engine reads or writes the H.264 path's address registers in JPEG
mode is not documented: an encoder reset clears them, and behind the
IOMMU an access through 0 stalls the engine, so they all name one
scratch buffer the size of a reconstructed picture.

Both encoders now take NV21, YUV420 and YVU420 as well as NV12, through
the input stage format codes of the V3s register map (4 for NV21, 24 for
three planes; YVU420 is the three-plane code with the chroma plane
addresses swapped). The input stage programming moves to cedrus_enc.c
for both. The media controller entities of an encoder video device are
now a struct, one set per encoder device.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
